= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @authoritarian: The authoritarian parties of the right and left - the KPP, and ChZJN.
- @false_left: The false left - the KPP and NPR.
- @chzjn: The bourgeoise - ChZJN.
- @kpp: The KPP.
- @foreign: Perhaps we can target Foreign Powers?
- @easy_discard

@authoritarian
on-arrival: enemies = "authoritarian"; center_strength += 5; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 5; workers_kpd -= 2; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 2; kpd_relation -= 10

Attacking the far right and left is popular among all but the left wing of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the bourgeois parties. This might also hamper our ability to reconcile with the KPD in the future.

@false_left
on-arrival: enemies = "false left"; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3;

Attacking the far right is popular among the entire party, although the left considers the bourgeois parties to be just as dangerous, while the right is critical of our lack of response to the KPD. Our bourgeois coalition partners are also skeptical of our lack of commitment to anti-communism.

@chzjn
on-arrival: enemies = "ChZJN"; neorevisionist_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_r < 10 : The NSDAP is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and nsdap_r >= 10 : The Nazis are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@kpp
on-arrival: enemies = "KPP"; internationalist_dissent += 4; center_dissent -= 5; nationalist_dissent -= 5; kpp_relation -= 10; psl_w_relation += 5; psl_p_relation += 5; workers_kpp -= 6;

Attacking the KPP is supported by all but the most left-wing socialists, and wins us some measure of approval among the bourgeois parties. However, If we are to reconcile with the KPP, this may not be the best choice.

@foreign
on-arrival: enemies = "foreign powers"; nationalist_strength += 5; nationalist_dissent -= 5; germany_relation -= 2; soviet_relation -= 2; psl_p_relation += 2; npr_relation += 3; zln_relation += 2; internationalist_dissent += 8; nationalism += 3; peasants_pps += 4; petit_pps += 3;

Our anti-nationalist rhetoric is popular among the nationalist, but may make it harder to build the relations with them that are necessary for diplomacy in the future.
